-- title:
--   Right invariance of the unipotent adelic measure on GL₃
-- statement:
--   Work over the adele ring $\mathbb{A} =$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ` of $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra and with the additive Haar measure `adelicAddHaar (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ`, and inside $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A})$ equipped with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra. For $x,y,z \in \mathbb{A}$ let $n(x,y,z) = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & x & z \\ 0 & 1 & y \\ 0 & 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$ be the invertible matrix `upperUnipotent3 x y z` (with the explicit inverse having entries $-x$, $xy-z$, $-y$), and let `unipotentSubgroup3` be the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A})$ generated by the set of all such $n(x,y,z)$, carrying the subtype Borel structure. The measure `unipotentHaar3` on this subgroup is the pushforward, along $(x,y,z) \mapsto n(x,y,z)$ viewed as an element of the subgroup, of the threefold product $\mu \times (\mu \times \mu)$ of the adelic additive Haar measure $\mu$ on $\mathbb{A}^3$. The theorem asserts that this measure is invariant under right translation: for every element $n_0$ of `unipotentSubgroup3`, the pushforward of `unipotentHaar3` along $n \mapsto n n_0$ equals `unipotentHaar3`.
--
--   This is the right-invariance half of the statement that the transported product measure on the upper unipotent subgroup $N(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ is a Haar measure, i.e. that $N(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ is unimodular with this normalisation. It is used in the integration estimates for Whittaker functions on $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over the adeles, for instance in the computation of integrals over the zeroth shell in terms of integrals over the torus and in the orthogonality and Bessel-type inequalities for the cubic induction.
